    "js": 0,
    "css": 3072,
    "image": 0,
    "font": 102400,
    "animation": 0,
    "enhancement": 0
  },
  "fallbacks": [
    "Each shipped family is followed by metric-matched fallback faces over local system fonts (size-adjust and ascent, descent, and line-gap overrides), then a system stack and a generic family.",
    "There's a fallback face at each weight the roles set, over the system bold for a heading.",
    "Glyphs outside every shipped face's unicode-range render in the declared system stack, so text never goes missing."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "IBM Plex Mono ships at 400, for captions and code, and 500, for labels and numerals, and covers Latin-1 at both; its Latin Extended split ships at 400 alone, so a label's or numeral's extended letters, such as ő or ł, set in Plex 400.",
    "Space Grotesk ships upright only, as upstream draws it: em in running text renders as a slanted upright.",
    "Space Grotesk's and Plex's latin-ext subsets (18,940 B and 13,260 B) load only on a page whose text needs them; a Latin page loads 57,700 B. Other scripts render in the declared system stack."
  ],
